or infertility."]},{"sid":39541,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never.","Alcohol: None.","Occupation: High school student; competitive athlete (basketball and tennis)."]},{"sid":39542,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On physical examination, his pubertal development is Tanner stage V.","The right testis is normal in size and consistency.","The left testis is soft and appears smaller.","Palpation of the left scrotum while the patient is standing reveals a soft, compressible mass that increases with Valsalva maneuver and decreases when lying down.","The mass does not transilluminate and is described by the examiner as feeling like a collection of tangled cords.","Cremasteric reflex is intact bilaterally, and there are no signs of inflammation or masses within the testes themselves."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10386,"date":"2020-05-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Pediatrics","attending":"Dr. Michael Okonkwo","cc":"Routine health maintenance visit with parental concerns regarding behavioral changes including declining grades, increased secrecy, and suspected substance use.","order":1,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[2595],"sections":[{"sid":39543,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Routine health maintenance visit with parental concerns regarding behavioral changes including declining grades, increased secrecy, and suspected substance use."]},{"sid":39544,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns for routine health maintenance approximately four months following his prior urology evaluation for left-sided varicocele.","The parents express concern about recent changes in their son's behavior, including declining grades, increased secrecy, and a new peer group.","They request that he be drug tested without his knowledge, stating they suspect he may be using illicit substances.","After speaking with the parents, permission is obtained to speak with the patient privately.","During the private conversation, the patient denies any drug use and appears to be forthcoming.","He expresses stress about school and a recent breakup with his girlfriend."]},{"sid":39545,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Left-sided varicocele (diagnosed 2020-01-15)"]},{"sid":39546,"type":"psh","lines":["- None"]},{"sid":39547,"type":"medications","lines":["He takes no medications"]},{"sid":39548,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":39549,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Father with major depressive disorder","- Paternal grandmother with breast cancer (diagnosed age 52)"]},{"sid":39550,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never.","Alcohol: None.","Occupation: High school student; competitive athlete (basketball and tennis)."]},{"sid":39551,"type":"vitals","lines":["His vital signs are within normal limits"]},{"sid":39552,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, the patient appears well-groomed, is cooperative, and shows no signs of acute distress.","The physical examination is unremarkable."]},{"sid":39553,"type":"other_studies","lines":["He agrees to a confidential depression screening, which reveals mild depressive symptoms."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10384,"date":"2020-10-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Orthopedic Surgery","attending":"Dr. Jennifer Walsh","cc":"Three months of progressive right knee pain that worsens at night and with physical activity, recently resulting in a limp during basketball practice.","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[6910],"sections":[{"sid":39554,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Three months of progressive right knee pain that worsens at night and with physical activity, recently resulting in a limp during basketball practice."]},{"sid":39555,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient with history of varicocele and behavioral evaluation presents with knee pain that worsens at night and with physical activity.","He reports intermittent swelling and has recently developed a limp during basketball practice.","There is no history of trauma, fever, or weight loss."]},{"sid":39556,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Left-sided varicocele (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Mild depressive episode amenable to psychotherapy alone (diagnosed 2020-05-15)"]},{"sid":39557,"type":"psh","lines":["- None"]},{"sid":39558,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":39559,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Father with major depressive disorder","- Paternal grandmother with breast cancer (diagnosed age 52)"]},{"sid":39560,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never.","Alcohol: None.","Occupation: High school student; competitive athlete (basketball and tennis)."]},{"sid":39561,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, there is a firm, tender mass over the distal anterior thigh with mild warmth and decreased range of motion at the knee."]},{"sid":39562,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory studies reveal elevated alkaline phosphatase and lactate dehydrogenase levels."]},{"sid":39563,"type":"imaging","lines":["Radiographs of the distal femur show a destructive metaphyseal lesion with mixed radiodensity, periosteal new bone formation in a \"sunburst\" pattern, and a triangular elevation of the periosteum adjacent to the lesion.","MRI demonstrates cortical destruction and a soft-tissue mass."]},{"sid":39564,"type":"pathology","lines":["A biopsy is performed and histology reveals pleomorphic tumor cells producing osteoid."]},{"sid":39565,"type":"assessment","lines":["After discussing typical patterns of location, the oncologic team explains that the most common site of this tumor is the distal femur."]}],"orders":[{"order_id":1210,"modality":"xray","region":"extremity_lower","indication":"Right knee pain","provider":"Dr. Jennifer Walsh","priority":"urgent","datetime":"2020-10-15","result_sid":39563}]},{"id":10387,"date":"2021-01-15","type":"ed","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. David Kim","cc":"Progressive right knee pain and swelling now accompanied by low-grade fever over the past few weeks.","order":3,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[2819],"secti